.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt PAX 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm pax
.Nd read and write POSIX pax archives
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl w|a|r|x|t
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl p
.Fl f Ar archive
.Op Ar paths ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility reads and writes POSIX pax archives: ustar headers with
.Ql x
extended-header records for paths, link paths, large sizes and negative
mtimes. Regular files, directories and symbolic links are supported.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl w
Write the named paths to a new archive.
.It Fl a
Append the named paths to an existing archive.
.It Fl r
Read and extract.
.It Fl x
Extract.
.It Fl t
List.
.It Fl v
Verbose list/extract.
.It Fl p
Preserve modes (extraction restores stored modes).
.It Fl f Ar archive
Archive file.
.El
.Pp
Extended records use the
.Ql <length> <keyword>=<value>
form. Compression
.Pq Fl z , Fl j , Fl J
is not supported and is a usage error.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A malformed archive or unsafe path exits with status 1; a usage error exits with status 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr tar 1 ,
.Xr ar 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD implements the pax extended-header subset described above.
